The prompt's output path apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/VehicleSystems/** is a real, compiled project.yml
source group: both app targets (TeslaSync iOS, TeslaSync-macOS) list `- path: TeslaSync/Features`
(excluding *Tests.swift), alongside the sibling System/ and Telemetry/ feature pages already shipping there.
The page ships exactly at the prompt path. Strings ship in the platform catalog
apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings (an allowed file). xcodegen rebuilds the git-ignored
TeslaSync.xcodeproj; "MediaPlayer" is referenced 60x in the regenerated pbxproj (iOS + macOS app + both
test bundles).

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route /media-player gets a dedicated AppRoute.mediaPlayer case (pathSegment
"media-player", Vehicle group, SF Symbol music.note). AppRouteParser already resolves /media-player ->
.mediaPlayer by pathSegment match (deep link). MediaPlayerRouteRegistration registers MediaPlayerPage on
.mediaPlayer, chained into \.routeHosts in TeslaSyncApp.swift, so the page is reachable from the
Vehicle-group sidebar entry, the iPhone More list, the Navigate menu (auto-derived), and the
/media-player deep link. (Navigation registration is an allowed file per the prompt.) ExploreCatalog and
MenuCommandCatalog both derive from AppRoute.allCases, so the new route flows into the feature hub and the
Navigate menu automatically — no manual catalog edit needed.

UNITS: media values are dimensionless counts (unique tracks, source counts, volume on a 0..max scale) and
millisecond play time — none are SI physical quantities, so no SI conversion applies (ADR-005 is a no-op
here); the display boundary only formats counts, play time (m:ss), and timestamps.

